source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: The cell keeps reading past the forced newline: Jira renders one data cell holding a level-1 heading whose text is `x` and a forced newline, and a paragraph `y` below that heading inside the same cell. jiro reads the row across both lines and keeps the whole table as raw Jira Markup, which a GFM cell could hold none of.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|h1. x\\
y|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><h1><a name="x%5C%5C"></a>x<br class="atl-forced-newline" /></h1>
<p>y</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|h1. x\\
y|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
